    "body": "EICMA 2026 • Yamaha Previews the Future of the Tenere Adventure Bikes With Mysterious 4 Concept\nNew G65 BMW X5 Gets Visited by the Tuning Fairy, Is This a Good Look for the Neue Klasse Model?\n7 photos\nPhoto: Instagram | waido.kits\nThe paint has barely dried on the body of the new-generation BMW X5 , but the model has already been visited by the tuning fairy. And no, it’s not a CGI-infused makeover this time around, as you too could make your very own example look exactly like this.\nSigned by @waido.kits and shared on social media a few days ago, this is the final design of their body kit, which includes the usual add-ons on the outside. It is offered as a bundle, though interested parties can also order some of these parts individually. And if you must know, the company is already accepting pre-orders.\nThe makeover certainly makes the G65 BMW X5 a lot more visible. Not that it flies under the radar, as the Neue Klasse look has created what is arguably the most controversial X5 ever. Therefore, a few aftermarket tweaks could be just what the doctor ordered in order to make the entire thing more appealing from a visual perspective. However, the pictured example hasn’t been “tweaked,” but modified to the point where it looks a lot more aggressive.\nActually, “pictured” may not be the best word to describe it, because “rendered” would suit it much better. That’s because the makeover may be real, and available for pre-order as we speak, as mentioned above, but the car in question does not exist outside Fantasy Land. Nevertheless, it does reveal what your tuned X5 from the new generation could look for, if you settle for these upgrades, in these color combinations.\nPhoto: Instagram | waido.kits So, what is new, you ask? Well, the hood for one, which features some extra bulges on it. The add-ons on the sides of the front bumper have also come from the aftermarket world, and so has the new splitter, which looks very sporty. The grille appears to have been tweaked as well, and the changes do not end here.\nFar from it, actually, because this new-gen BMW X5 also benefits from fender flares. The wheel arch attachments have made it a lot wider than before, and we can also see that there are new side skirt add-ons on deck, too, as part of the visual makeover, as well as panels on the lower parts of the doors, right above the side skirts.\nAt the rear, this machine sports a new diffuser, as well as some extras on the sides of the bumper, as well as what seems to be a new roof-mounted spoiler. The lighting units on the outside have been tinted, and so have the windows. Some of the new components are presented in glossy black, others have been virtually painted in the same color as the rest of the body, whereas some have a forged carbon look.\nThese include the wheel arch attachments and the hood, and due to these, the BMW X5 in question sends some Mansory vibes. In my opinion, anyway. The premium mid-size crossover also sits a lot closer to the ground, so the suspension has been altered, at least in these digital illustrations. The wheels are new, have a concave design, and are a two-tone proposal.\nPhoto: Instagram | waido.kits Waido’s name decorates the tailgate in the renderings shared in our gallery, and the tuner says that the extras mentioned above can be equipped to all G65s, as well as they feature the M Package . And just so you know, in addition to carbon fiber, which is a must-have when it comes to high-end modern-day tuning jobs, some of the add-ons have been made of ABS plastic.\nA power boost is not part of the makeover, so we will remind you that the 40 and 40 xDrive versions of the Neue Klasse BMW X5 are offered with a 3.0-liter TwinPower Turbo engine. The straight-six mill produces 394 hp (294 kW/400 ps), enabling 0-60 mph (0-97 kph) in 5.2 and 5.1 seconds, respectively.\nThe plug-in hybrid model , which is known as the X5 50E xDrive, is faster. It deals with the 0-60 mph sprint in 4.6 seconds, aided by the 483 horsepower (360 kW/490 ps) produced in total by the electrified inline-six. It is just as punchy and fast as its predecessor, though it can now travel up to 44 miles (71 km) on zero emissions instead of 39 miles (63 km).\nPricing for the 2027 BMW X5 starts at $69,800 for the base 40 model in the States, and the 40 xDrive is available from $72,100. As for the PHEV, you are looking at a minimum of $77,500, excluding destination, options, and dealer fees.\nWaido hasn’t said anything about the pricing part when it comes to its tuning bundle for the G65 BMW X5 , though it invites interested parties to reach out to them in order to discuss the details. Does this look suit the new X5? Drop a line below and tell us all about it. View this post on Instagram A post shared by WAIDO | Sculpted for distinction (@waido.kits) View this post on Instagram A post shared by WAIDO | Sculpted for distinction (@waido.kits)\nLiked the article? Follow us to see more stories from autoevolution in your Google feeds.\nbmw x5 BMW X5 2027 bmw x5 tuning crossover\nAbout the author: Cristian Gnaticov\nAfter a series of unfortunate events put an end to Cristian's dream of entering a custom built & tuned old-school Dacia into a rally competition, he moved on to drive press cars and write for a living. He's worked for several automotive online journals and now he's back at autoevolution after his first tour in the mid-2000s. Full profile\nUP NEXT All-New 2028 BMW M6 Neue Klasse Takes the Fifth-Gen 6 Series Back in Time to the E24 Age – Rendering",
